Feature 1 (CV for sorting): While industrial CV sorting exists, and some apps advise on recycling, a robust in-app CV for household/small-scale waste sorting guidance with high accuracy is still a niche or emerging area for consumer apps. This would be a strong differentiator.

Feature 2 (Dynamic Channeling based on waste type): While route optimization is common, the real-time, waste-type-dependent channeling directly linked to user input (from image uploads) would be an advanced form of dynamic dispatch.

Feature 3 (Environmental Contribution & Rewards via Image): The reward system is existing, and environmental impact calculation is emerging. However, the direct trigger of these rewards based on image uploads and CV-driven estimation is a novel integration.

Feature 4 (Optimized Routes for Collectors with Presorted Delivery): This is a well-established and critical component of professional waste management software, but integrating it seamlessly with the preceding user-generated data (classified waste, pickup requests) would create a powerful end-to-end solution.
